WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.424
In Qin's final years, people everywhere rose up against its tyranny.

00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:11.660
In the villages, people raised torches and banners, full of hope.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.688
Liu Bang led his army and set out for Guanzhong.

00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:20.172
The soldiers' morale was high, their banners flying in the wind.

00:00:20.672 --> 00:00:26.600
In 206 BCE, Ziying, the King of Qin, surrendered to Liu Bang.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:33.484
Ziying knelt and handed the emperor's seal to Liu Bang — and with that, Qin fell.

00:00:33.984 --> 00:00:37.776
The Qin palaces stood empty as power changed hands peacefully.

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:42.548
Liu Bang agreed with the people on three simple articles of law.

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:46.624
The people cheered, welcoming a new age.

00:00:47.124 --> 00:00:54.940
Far away, the banners of Liu Bang and Xiang Yu faced each other — a new struggle was about to begin.
